0..76 Comment "// The pure λ-calculus as data and its single substitution, the base of the"
77..151 Comment "// λ-calculus syntax model (#640). `theory LC` is the single-substitution"
152..229 Comment "// calculus of Kaposi and Xie (_Second-Order Generalised Algebraic Theories_,"
230..299 Comment "// FSCD 2024, doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10, §7): the presentation"
300..374 Comment "// `first_order` mints from `theory Lambda`, its names written without the"
375..447 Comment "// generated `$` and its context arguments implicit, as a `theory` block"
448..522 Comment "// writes them (#765). The syntax model\'s carriers are de Bruijn terms and"
523..598 Comment "// two substitution data: a substitution shifts, conses a term onto another"
599..675 Comment "// or lifts one under a binder, and a renaming shifts or lifts. Lifting is a"
676..751 Comment "// constructor and every lookup a tail call, so the substitution laws reach"
752..798 Comment "// their inductive steps by conversion (#761)."
799..801 Comment "//"
802..877 Comment "// The argument, file by file: this base; the laws that hold by computation"
878..954 Comment "// (`sub-q-single`, `sub-q-lift`, `sub-lam`, `sub-app`); the congruences and"
955..1028 Comment "// the lemmas laws 3 and 4 are proved from (`congruence`, `shift-lookup`,"
1029..1096 Comment "// `rename-rename`, `lookup-weaken`, `subst-rename`, `subst-subst`,"
1097..1164 Comment "// `subst-id`, `subst-as-rename`); laws 3 and 4 (`sub-weaken-lift`,"
1165..1241 Comment "// `sub-weaken-single`); the syntax model (`syntax-model`) and the record of"
1242..1290 Comment "// `LC`\'s models it packs into (`model-record`)."
1292..1331 Comment "// The naturals, the de Bruijn indices."
1332..1338 Keyword "import"
1339..1340 StringLit "\""
1340..1364 StringLit "../model-in-source.gandr"
1364..1365 StringLit "\""
1366..1367 Other ";"
1369..1440 Comment "/// The single-substitution calculus of the pure λ-calculus: contexts,"
1441..1514 Comment "/// substitutions between them and terms in a context; the empty context,"
1515..1590 Comment "/// substitution, context extension, weakening, the newest variable, single"
1591..1657 Comment "/// substitution and lifting; abstraction and application; the six"
1658..1729 Comment "/// substitution laws. Its rules over the indexed sorts are outside the"
1730..1792 Comment "/// fragment (#522); `Model(LC)` derives from it all the same."
